in about two months we'll all be playing  cicchitto a game that's really shaking  the foundations of the souls born  franchise and the hardest thing for this  community to wrap its head around has  been the lack of RPG elements cicchitto  has no stat level up screen you're  forced to use a katana and there are  fewer gear choices but recently it has  been revealed that Sookie Rose still has  a surprising amount of character  customization no you can't dress up as  an onion of the day poor princess  Lautrec but you can level up your  character you can diversify your play  style and you can even spec into  different combos and special attacks  this is all done for the first time with  something simply called  experience as you kill enemies you'll  rack up experience points which actually  aren't lost upon death unlike in other  souls games once you have enough you  head back to the hub world and then you  invest them into three talent trees one  of these trees is called shinobi another  one is called prosthetic and the third  is called samurai it reminds me a lot of  World of Warcraft's old talent system  you know back when World of Warcraft  didn't feel like a mobile game so just  like this actually these talent trees  will contain both active abilities that  you can unlock and also passive effects  that you can invest in so let's take the  shinobi talent tree for example from  what I understand this would enhance  things like your critical strikes your  stealth basically everything assassin  related take wall-jumping for example  this would be an example of a active  ability and an example of a passive  shinobi ability might be reducing your  aggro range during stealth something  like that I'm sure you guys can think of  more second the prosthetic talent tree  this one's pretty self-explanatory an  active ability in this tree might be  unlocking combo attacks for your  prosthetics like how flame vent can set  your sword on fire or how your shuriken  arm can follow up with a katana  a passive effect in this tree would be  increasing the amount of shriek ins  thrown for example as seen here or maybe  reducing the amount of spirit emblems  you need to activate an attack and third  the samurai talent tree which I think  will be my favorite is likely going to  focus on general combat so in terms of  active abilities we know already that  there are special attacks that you can  perform by holding down r1 and l1 like  this cross slash attack for example so I  bet there will be tons of other  varieties to unlock in this tree an  example of a passive ability in this  tree might be making you deal more  posture damage or allowing your healing  gourd to replenish more health and  apparently with another experience you  can actually upgrade every talent in  this tree and 100% complete your  character but it's unlikely that you'll  be able to do this in a single  playthrough and experience isn't the  only form of currency there's also gold  another static resource that we use to  trade with vendors there's even  apparently crafting materials that we  can use to enhance our prosthetic arm so  this is pretty great the more you  explore the world the more enemies you  fight and the more you enhance your  character and diversify your play style  you can lament the loss of a stat system  or you like really but you kind of have  to admit grinding for a new attack or a  new skill it's a bit more exciting than  grinding to upgrade one point of  dexterity not that I leveled X or  anything leveling up is done at the hub  location which is called the dilapidated  temple a place located on the Agena  outskirts and like in other games npcs  will occasionally travel here for quests  or for trading but we already know of  three who will be there every time  first the sculptor as expected he's the  one we go to to upgrade our prosthetic  arm with materials that we find  throughout the world  second there's going to be a woman there  named Emma she's responsible for  upgrading the amount of charges your  healing gourd can contain upgraded with  an item called  spirit water drops and third and my  favorite the immortal soldier I love  this basically his a swordsman  that's incapable of dying and so he  serves as a sort of human training dummy  who we can whale on and practice our  move set with I really hope he wins is  about it like crestfallen would I have a  feeling that'll be the same sort of  character and being able to practice  combat here is way way way more  important in cicchitto than it has been  in other souls games because in  cicchitto the hub will also be the place  where we invest in skill trees and  abilities that fundamentally change the  way our character plays so it makes  sense to be able to test these in a safe  environment outside of the talent tree  if you want a permanent upgrade to your  health or posture this is done through  an item called prayer beads apparently  these are commonly dropped by mini  bosses in cicchitto and that's a good  reason to fight these mini bosses  instead of running past them because yes  running past things is probably gonna be  pretty effective in this game  according to Miyazaki the environments  are fairly open in the beginning but he  also said that they really open up  around the halfway mark in the game and  open up they should because not only can  we grapple over things we can swim  that's right  no longer do we need to fear knee-deep  water imagine sneaking into a castle via  a water duct or fighting a boss that  swims beneath you  in Game Informer's two-hour session  sekito explored the Hirata  estates and the name Hirata should be  familiar to some of you who watched this  video apparently we travel back to this  place in a memory and this is accessed  via the hub world which raises the  question by visiting this memory are we  simply reliving something that has  already happened or are we capable of  going back in time to change the past  and considering we still have our ninja  prosthetic in all of these scenes I'm  leaning towards the latter I think we  might be able to change things here the  village is being razed to the ground  by drunken bandits I can't wait to  figure out why second mini-bosses of  this stage is one of these drunken  bandits  his name is Jews oh the drunkard in his  second phase he spits poison onto his  weapon which means it will probably  damage you if you try to parry him and  this is a cool example of how they can  subvert the core gameplay in cicchitto  because everyone's playing in a similar  way so everyone is going to have to find  a way around this regardless of your  built apparently during this mini boss  you can find a nearby NPC who will help  you during this fight but since there's  no summoning system in sukira you know  there's no one line there's no soap  stones or anything reports say that if  this NPC dies during the fight it might  be permanent not everyone is undead this  time you have to remember and the  concept of death permanence in cicchitto  for NPCs at least could mark a pretty  huge departure from all of the years and  years of undead characters we've had  with souls games in those games it was  often difficult to pin down a canon  death for the character but in cicchitto  with well-defined death comes more  emotional stories and speaking of  emotion apparently some of these NPCs  now have their own soundtracks  we've known for a while that the music  is being composed by the legendary  Yukari Tamura who has done in-house  music for many from games before this  and she's going to have her hands full  because there's more music in this game  than in any other previous title not  only is that the music for boss battles  there is music during stealth during  combat during exploration and there are  even songs created for specific  characters said to enhance the emotions  associated with their stories and as  someone who spends hours and hours  finding the perfect music to suit these  characters in prepare to cry this last  point makes me pretty excited think how  fitting  Gwyn's theme is for his character and  then apply that to some of your  favourite characters in these games they  kind of all deserve all of this pales in  comparison  perhaps the biggest news this week  cicchitto has a pause button I'll just  let that sink in a bit it actually makes  more sense in this game since sake dough  is about killing ingeniously you can  apparently pause and get an opportunity  to rifle through your equipment and your  items for a solution to your problem the  biggest curiosity that remains I think  is the death penalty Miyazaki himself  recently said that it's still taking  shape and it's very unique and it's more  personal than ever before and he also  said that it's not just going to be the  classic corpse run to retrieve your  souls  so what could it be I want you guys to  help me out with this one  I reckon together we'll probably stumble  across it so here are my current ideas  first since Miyazaki says that the death  penalty for dying is more personal then  I think perhaps it's our prince who is  keeping us alive with his blood our  prince after all in the last trailer  said wolf along with my blood you must  live I wouldn't be surprised if with  every death we weaken our Prince or  perhaps with every death we develop a  more difficult world state you know just  like world tendency in Demon Souls  perhaps enemies grow stronger every time  we die since we pray to these statues  which are called demon Buddha statues  what if sukira himself becomes more  demon like with every death imagine a  sort of deal with the devil every time  you die and finally blood-borne had an  insight meter what if our perception of  the world changes negatively with every  death these are some ideas can you think  of others let me know in the comments  below and if you're watching this video  as it goes live right now chances are  I'm streaming right now so come over to  twitch and say hi I'll see you all next  time  [Music]
 

